      "content": "There are inherent risks when transitioning from probabilistic modeling to a deterministic rule-based system, which include a possible loss in the model's ability to anticipate and adapt to unforeseen anomalies. Reliance on historical data and predefined rules could lead to increased false positives or negatives if the rules aren't sufficiently comprehensive or adaptable to variations in telemetry data. We'll mitigate against this by conducting a thorough validation phase, comparing outputs of both models on historical cases to ensure consistent performance, followed by gradual real-world testing. Moreover, any blind spots can be addressed through manual oversight and continuous updates of the rule-based systems by expert engineers who can incorporate new insights and emerging issues identified during the initial phase of the legacy engine deployment.",
